      "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09722",
      "contributions": [
        "The supplied search summary describes excessive recency emphasis and reported improvements from mitigating it.",
        "Motivates measuring recency reliance without assuming stronger reliance is beneficial."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not validate the proposed sensitivity probe or establish improvements on the pinned four-category RecHarness task."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[2] Liu et al., RecSys 2025: item-availability confounding in history shuffling",
      "link": "https://doi.org/10.1145/3705328.3748042",
      "contributions": [
        "The supplied summary distinguishes user-order effects from item-availability effects using constrained shuffling.",
        "Motivates explicit chronology and careful interpretation of history perturbations."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Availability-aware shuffling does not remove positional, repetition, or plausibility confounds in deletion interventions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[3] Petrov et al. (2026): Do Sequential Recommendation Benchmarks Require Higher-Order Sequence Modelling?",
      "link": "https://research.atspotify.com/2026/10/do-sequential-recommendation-benchmarks-require-higher-order-sequence-modelling",
      "contributions": [
        "The supplied summary reports history-aware pairwise models outperforming SASRec and eSASRec reproductions on four of five benchmarks using NDCG@10.",
        "Separates earlier-history, recency-weighting, and joint-contextualization contributions and motivates simple transition controls."
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Does not establish gains under the pinned sampled HR@10 protocol or validate sensitivity as a model-selection predictor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "[4] TREC 2025 Recommendation Guidelines",
